tom@soda.berkeley.edu (Tom Holub) writes:
>dif@bhprtc.scpd.oz.au (David Faulkner) writes:
>
>If you don't polypile (I usually don't), the wand is useful.  All you
>really need to win is the following (newbies take note)
>
>-15 AC
>+6 or better Excalibur, Mjollnir, Fire or Frost Brand, maybe even Stormy.
>Teleport Control
>Levitation
>Poison Resistance
>Magic Resistance

That's misleading.  

I've never won with AC better than -8. 
  (I only like temple priests for their spellbooks.) 
I've almost never had a +6 weapon. 
  (Good strength makes up for the damage bonus.)

You also *need* fire resistance.
You are better off with telepathy. (blindfold & mirror, too.)
You don't *need* magic resistance.  (But you're better off with it.)
You don't *need* levitation, either. (But you're better off with it.)
  (The only time levitation comes in handy is on the way back up in
   the corridor in the strong-hold.  And there are ways around this.)
  (All the other barriers are water, and usually only one square big.)          

My personal list of additional things I like before I get too deep:
+ A rustproof primary weapon.  (Otherwise, a unicorn horn will do.)
+ Some kind of cloak or reflection to spare my armor from bad breath.
+ Speed. (Marginal is ok, but speed boots are preferable.)
+ Ring of conflict. ("Destroy the thief,...")

